WEBVTT

00:00:00.591 --> 00:00:01.550
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.656 --> 00:00:04.990
Today, we are talking about the cut that seems the easiest:

00:00:05.199 --> 00:00:07.070
the one-length cut, and the bob.

00:00:07.579 --> 00:00:09.550
All the hair falls to the same line.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:10.670
No layers.

00:00:10.937 --> 00:00:15.182
But precisely because there is only a single line, if it is even slightly off,

00:00:15.132 --> 00:00:17.710
the client sees it in the mirror straight away.

00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:21.710
A beautiful bob line is the result of a lot of small details.

00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:27.558
A one-length cut means every strand, falling naturally, stops at the same line.

00:00:28.056 --> 00:00:31.142
That line can be at the shoulders, at the collarbone,

00:00:31.092 --> 00:00:32.917
or as short as around the chin.

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.757
Cut as short as around the chin, it is usually called a bob.

00:00:37.181 --> 00:00:39.877
From behind, the line is straight across.

00:00:40.145 --> 00:00:43.237
From the side, the line runs parallel to the floor.

00:00:43.582 --> 00:00:46.517
The ends are thick, heavy, and shiny.

00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:49.578
There are three bob shapes you will often see.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.178
The one-length bob:

00:00:51.354 --> 00:00:54.058
a straight, even line, as we just saw.

00:00:54.488 --> 00:00:55.738
The A-line bob:

00:00:55.927 --> 00:00:58.778
shorter at the back, getting longer toward the face.

00:00:59.127 --> 00:01:00.618
The cutting line is a diagonal.

00:01:01.192 --> 00:01:05.578
And the bob with graduation at the nape, which many places call a graduated bob.

00:01:06.008 --> 00:01:09.169
The nape is cut with a low elevation, so the hair stacks,

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:11.898
building a rounded volume at the back of the head.

00:01:12.153 --> 00:01:14.437
This lesson focuses on the one-length bob,

00:01:14.387 --> 00:01:16.778
because it is the foundation for the others.

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:21.738
As for the names, every place and every school uses slightly different ones.

00:01:22.354 --> 00:01:27.197
Before cutting, do the consultation, as in the consultation and sectioning lesson.

00:01:27.674 --> 00:01:32.378
With a bob, it is even more important to agree on the length very clearly,

00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:35.837
because going from long hair to a bob is a huge change.

00:01:36.239 --> 00:01:40.397
Hold a section of hair, fold it up to exactly the spot, and ask:

00:01:40.663 --> 00:01:43.757
we are cutting to here, at the chin, is that right?

00:01:44.012 --> 00:01:48.637
Also ask whether the client often tucks her hair behind her ears, or ties it up.

00:01:49.082 --> 00:01:52.957
With a chin-length bob, she will hardly be able to tie it up anymore.

00:01:53.621 --> 00:01:55.273
Then read the client's build.

00:01:55.699 --> 00:01:57.593
A long neck, or a short neck:

00:01:58.081 --> 00:02:01.113
where the bob line stops on the neck is where the eye stops.

00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:03.193
Look at the hairline at the nape.

00:02:03.565 --> 00:02:06.804
If there is a whorl at the nape, with hair growing upward,

00:02:06.754 --> 00:02:09.993
a bob line that is too short at the nape easily kicks out.

00:02:10.412 --> 00:02:13.193
Keep the line below the whorl, or a little longer.

00:02:13.536 --> 00:02:14.793
And watch the shoulders.

00:02:15.021 --> 00:02:19.128
Hair that stops right on the shoulders flicks out every time the client moves,

00:02:19.078 --> 00:02:20.793
as the ends touch the shoulders.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.833
So choose above the shoulders, or well past them.

00:02:24.461 --> 00:02:27.196
One-length hair is cut along its natural fall.

00:02:27.598 --> 00:02:32.636
Comb the hair straight down, exactly where it falls, at 0° elevation:

00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:34.236
not lifting the hair at all.

00:02:34.626 --> 00:02:36.156
Light, even tension.

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:40.812
Pull too tight, especially when the hair is wet, and once it dries,

00:02:40.762 --> 00:02:42.636
the hair shrinks up, shorter,

00:02:42.743 --> 00:02:43.516
and uneven.

00:02:43.856 --> 00:02:46.396
Straight hair also shrinks up a little as it dries.

00:02:46.663 --> 00:02:49.036
Wavy and curly hair shrink much more.

00:02:49.136 --> 00:02:53.175
So with curly hair, leave it longer than you intend, or cut it dry,

00:02:53.125 --> 00:02:55.676
with a technique you have been trained in.

00:02:56.299 --> 00:02:58.805
Section as always, clean and straight.

00:02:59.126 --> 00:03:02.725
Then start at the nape, with a very thin horizontal section.

00:03:03.061 --> 00:03:04.085
This is your guideline.

00:03:04.565 --> 00:03:09.285
Every layer after it is combed straight down, and cut exactly to this guideline.

00:03:09.713 --> 00:03:13.125
The guideline stays in one place, and the other layers come to it.

00:03:13.403 --> 00:03:15.365
It is called a stationary guideline.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:19.125
With thin sections, you can clearly see the guideline underneath.

00:03:19.372 --> 00:03:21.845
With sections that are too thick, you are guessing.

00:03:22.499 --> 00:03:24.905
The client's head position is very important.

00:03:25.383 --> 00:03:29.222
When cutting the nape, have the client tip her head forward slightly,

00:03:29.172 --> 00:03:30.265
chin a little down.

00:03:30.695 --> 00:03:35.385
The nape flattens, the hair lies close to the neck, and the line is easy to see.

00:03:35.737 --> 00:03:40.185
But however much she bends, when she lifts her head, the line changes with it.

00:03:40.532 --> 00:03:44.745
So bend moderately, and keep that same position until the back is finished.

00:03:44.984 --> 00:03:48.905
Before moving to the sides, have the client lift her head straight again.

00:03:49.168 --> 00:03:52.505
And remind her to sit up straight, without crossing her legs.

00:03:52.684 --> 00:03:56.105
Uneven shoulders and a tilted head mean an uneven line.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:59.238
On the sides, the tricky part is the ear.

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:02.358
The ear sticks out, and pushes the hair outward.

00:04:02.738 --> 00:04:06.692
If you pull the hair tight over the ear and cut, then when you let go,

00:04:06.642 --> 00:04:08.198
the ear pushes the hair up,

00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:10.198
leaving a gap right above the ear.

00:04:10.766 --> 00:04:15.471
So around the ear, comb the hair to fall naturally, and hold it very lightly,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.438
without tension.

00:04:17.175 --> 00:04:20.838
Some stylists support the hair with the comb against the skin before cutting.

00:04:21.457 --> 00:04:24.596
Checking is a job for the whole service, not just the end.

00:04:25.099 --> 00:04:28.116
After each side, compare both sides in the mirror:

00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:31.476
hold the two ends in front of the face, at the same height.

00:04:31.905 --> 00:04:35.076
The head must be straight, with the eyes looking straight ahead.

00:04:35.492 --> 00:04:39.636
Tilt the head a little, and the sides look uneven, even if you cut them correctly.

00:04:40.056 --> 00:04:43.396
Then look from behind, and from the side, on each side.

00:04:43.502 --> 00:04:47.316
The line must be continuous, with no corners and no steps.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.050
After blow-drying, check once more.

00:04:50.354 --> 00:04:53.890
Now, the hair lies exactly as the client will see it at home.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:57.890
If a few strands stick out, trim them lightly with the tips of the scissors.

00:04:58.235 --> 00:05:00.930
If the client likes softer ends, you can point cut:

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.530
turn the scissors up, and cut small notches into the ends.

00:05:04.799 --> 00:05:07.090
The line is less harsh, but keeps its shape.

00:05:07.275 --> 00:05:11.168
And if the client likes a crisp, sharp bob, keep the line blunt,

00:05:11.118 --> 00:05:12.370
and don't point cut.

00:05:13.024 --> 00:05:13.987
About safety.

00:05:14.428 --> 00:05:16.076
When cutting close to the neck,

00:05:16.026 --> 00:05:19.427
your fingers always stay between the blade and the client's skin.

00:05:20.008 --> 00:05:22.947
Never point the tips of the scissors toward the client's face.

00:05:23.294 --> 00:05:27.726
Scissors, combs and clips are cleaned and disinfected after every client,

00:05:27.676 --> 00:05:29.827
as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:05:30.256 --> 00:05:31.987
Neck strips are used only once.

00:05:32.609 --> 00:05:35.906
A beautiful bob line doesn't come from expensive scissors.

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:40.971
It comes from thin sections, light tension, the right head position,

00:05:40.921 --> 00:05:42.626
and checking many times.

00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:46.946
Every school and every country names and teaches this a little differently.

00:05:47.288 --> 00:05:48.866
This lesson is for practice;

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.506
it does not replace a professional qualification.

00:05:51.932 --> 00:05:55.586
In the practice lesson, we will cut it step by step, together.

00:05:55.843 --> 00:05:58.786
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:59.039 --> 00:05:59.746
See you next time.
